# Discrete joint motion. Field names and order follow the execution plan
# (docs/ROS2_头部与双臂控制_代码生成执行方案.md section 6) so that goal, result and
# feedback stay exactly as specified there.
#
# Semantics that the plan requires and this driver enforces:
#  * angle_rad is an OUTPUT SHAFT angle in radians; the driver converts with
#    round-half-away-from-zero to 0.1 deg and never multiplies by the gear ratio.
#  * motor_rpm is an ASSERTION about the speed the board already has stored for this
#    channel, NOT a speed command. The firmware takes speed from the stored per-channel
#    configuration (BSP/robot.c:334) and MOVE carries only the angle, so a goal cannot
#    change speed. 0 means "use whatever the board has"; a non-zero value that differs
#    from the board's stored rpm is REFUSED with error_code 111 and nothing is sent.
#    To change speed, run /robot/apply_config (whole board quiet, writes flash).
#  * RELATIVE needs position_valid unless allow_unreferenced_relative is enabled;
#    ABSOLUTE always needs position_valid. The check is made against a reading taken
#    by the worker immediately before the command, never against a published snapshot.
#  * limits_rad null means the mechanical limits are unconfirmed: motion is refused
#    with error_code 112 unless the node runs with commissioning:=true, and then each
#    command is capped and reported as having NO soft-limit protection.
#  * For BOTH modes the predicted endpoint is checked against limits_rad when the
#    limits are known and the position is trusted.
#  * A single MOVE is limited to +/-360 deg; larger goals are rejected, not split.
#  * timeout_sec is a monitoring deadline, not a promised arrival time.
#  * error_code carries the firmware business result 0..6, or a driver level code
#    (>=100) documented in ros2/README.md.
# Goal
uint8 RELATIVE=0
uint8 ABSOLUTE=1
string joint_name
uint8 mode
float64 angle_rad
uint16 motor_rpm
float64 timeout_sec
---
# Result
bool motion_completed
bool persisted
bool position_valid
uint16 error_code
string message
float64 final_angle_rad
---
# Feedback
uint16 command_sequence
uint8 state
uint8 fault
bool position_valid
bool brake
bool communication_ok
float64 current_angle_rad
float64 target_angle_rad
uint16 measured_motor_rpm
